      "description": "Watch Lille vs Estac Troyes highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 13, 2026. The Ligue 1 clash on September 13, 2026, delivered a captivating display of tactical discipline and clinical finishing. Both sides took to the pitch with high stakes, creating an atmosphere of anticipation as the match unfolded under the bright lights. Early Pressure and Breakthrough Lille ignited the contest with immediate attacking intent, nearly taking the lead in the 2nd minute when Dilane Bakwa saw his effort agonisingly strike the post. The drama intensified moments later as a Lille goal was chalked off following a VAR review for offside. Undeterred by the early setbacks, the home side continued to dictate play. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 18th minute; Tiago Santos unleashed a stunning right-footed strike from outside the penalty area, courtesy of a Dilane Bakwa assist, to give his side a deserved lead and settle the nerves of the home support. Tactical Shifts and Mbappe's Late Strike As the second half progressed, Troyes attempted to claw their way back into the game through a series of tactical substitutions, bringing on the likes of Renaud Ripart and Yacouba Kone . Lille countered by introducing veteran striker Olivier Giroud , who made his presence felt but earned a yellow card in the 82nd minute for a robust challenge. Despite Lille 's dominance in possession, which peaked at 64%, the result remained on a knife-edge until deep into stoppage time. In the 90+3rd minute, Maurits Kjaergaard turned provider for Ethan Mbappe , who clinicaly found the net with his left foot to secure the victory and ensure all three points stayed with the hosts."
